{"genre":"WritingPrompts","passages":[{"id":"T1","text":"I've always been baffled by those who feel the need to get drunk nightly. No amount of alcohol-induced bravery can mask the reality that they'll wake up the next day feeling just as broken inside. But I'm not without fault; I admit I misjudged someone last night.

Sitting around the big wooden table, listening to captivating stories of adventure, I was completely engrossed. Then, unexpectedly, a towering, muscular man at the far end of the bar began recounting his own grand adventures. His braggadocious narrative drew me in with each boastful detail. I couldn't help but chuckle silently at his youthful overstatements, feeling like I was part of a humorous tale. As he continued, my smile grew wider until I was thoroughly entertained by his yarn."},{"id":"T2","text":"I never grasped why folks insisted on getting hammered every night. No amount of liquid courage could alter the fact that you’re a wreck the next morning. As for me, I’m far from perfect, and I freely admit I misjudged the situation the previous evening.

I was so engrossed in swapping tales of daring deeds around the large wooden table that I didn’t notice a burly man at the bar's end launching into an epic narrative. Each boastful word drew me in, and I found myself smiling despite holding back laughter at his exaggerated tales. The more he spoke, the more I got swept up in the story, until I was thoroughly captivated."},{"id":"T3","text":"I have never understood why people want to get drunk every night. All the courage in the world can’t change the fact that the next morning you’re a broken man. But I’m not perfect, and I admit that I was a poor judge of character the night before. I was too distracted by all the fascinating stories being told around the big wooden table, when suddenly a tall, stout man at the end of the bar suddenly began to tell us an epic story of adventure. With every boastful word I grew more interested, I felt as if I were in the middle of a story, and I was the only one who didn’t laugh at the man’s childish exaggerations. The more he talked, the more I smiled, and soon I was completely engrossed in the story."},{"id":"T4","text":"I have never understood why people insist on getting drunk every night. All the courage in the world cannot change the fact that the next morning you are a broken man. But I am not perfect, and I admit that I was a poor judge of character the night before. I was too distracted by the fascinating stories that were being told around the big wooden table, when suddenly a tall, sturdy man at the end of the bar began to tell us an epic story of adventure. With every boastful word I became more and more interested, and I was the only one who did not laugh at the man’s childish exaggerations. The more he talked, the more I smiled, and soon I was completely absorbed in his story."}]}

