{"genre":"Essay","passages":[{"id":"T1","text":"Hyperlipidemia is characterized by excessively high levels of lipids, like cholesterol and triglycerides, in the bloodstream. These elevated levels increase the risk of coronary heart disease, including heart attacks and coronary artery disease. To combat this condition, various pharmaceutical options exist to help manage lipid levels and decrease the likelihood of heart disease.

