{"genre":"Essay","passages":[{"id":"T1","text":"The rise of digitalization and artificial intelligence (AI) has transformed supply chain management, fundamentally changing how goods are moved, monitored, and delivered. Known as Supply Chain 4.0, these technological advances have brought significant benefits but also challenges to the logistics sector. Additionally, the incorporation of predictive analytics through AI has refined route planning and boosted customer satisfaction. Meanwhile, the omnichannel model is reshaping traditional retail and supply chain practices across the globe.

Supply Chain 4.0 marks a major shift in supply chain management, using digital tools and AI to streamline operations, boost efficiency, and increase precision. Thanks to technologies such as the Internet of Things (IoT), cloud computing, and machine learning, businesses can now gather and analyze large volumes of data in real time, enhancing visibility and transparency throughout the supply chain."},{"id":"T2","text":"The rise of digitalization and artificial intelligence (AI) has significantly transformed supply chain management, fundamentally altering how goods move, are tracked, and reach their destinations. This latest phase of technological advancement, dubbed Supply Chain 4.0, brings both substantial advantages and challenges to the logistics sector. Additionally, the incorporation of predictive analytics systems powered by AI has greatly enhanced route planning and customer satisfaction.

Simultaneously, the omnichannel model has become a pivotal force in the global marketplace, redefining traditional retail and supply chain practices. Supply Chain 4.0 represents a major shift in how supply chains are managed, harnessing digitalization and AI to streamline operations, boost efficiency, and increase accuracy. Technologies such as the Internet of Things (IoT), cloud computing, and machine learning enable companies to gather and analyze large volumes of real-time data, thereby improving overall visibility and transparency across the supply chain."},{"id":"T3","text":"The advent of digitalization and the use of artificial intelligence has had a profound influence on the management of supply chains, revolutionizing the way goods are transported, tracked and delivered. This new wave of technological development, often called Supply Chain 4.0, has brought many benefits but also many challenges to the logistics industry. In addition, the integration of prediction systems based on artificial intelligence has improved route planning and customer satisfaction. At the same time, the omni-channel model has emerged as a disruptive force in the global market, reshaping the supply chain."},{"id":"T4","text":"The advent of digitalization and the use of artificial intelligence (AI) has had a profound effect on supply chain management, revolutionizing the way goods are transported, tracked and delivered. This new wave of technological development, often referred to as Supply Chain 4.0, has brought many benefits but also challenges to the logistics industry. Moreover, the integration of prediction systems based on artificial intelligence has improved route planning and increased customer satisfaction. In parallel, the omni-channel model has become a disruptive force in the global market, transforming the way goods are sold and delivered. Supply Chain 4.0 is a paradigm shift in the way supply chains are managed, combining digitalization and AI to optimize operations, improve efficiency and increase accuracy. With the help of the Internet of Things, cloud computing and machine learning, companies can now collect and analyze vast amounts of data in real time, resulting in greater visibility and transparency throughout the supply chain."}]}

